Version 0.3 and 0.4 (LIF Neurons and Training Investigation)
Version 0.3 aur 0.4 mein humne previous multimodal Spiking VGG-13 architecture ko continue kiya, lekin is baar focus model ki training stability, neuron behavior aur output spike generation par tha. Dataset ki 11 classes aur dono image modalities same rakhi gayi. Architecture mein ek additional average pooling operation introduce hua, jis se har branch ke features 32,768 se reduce hokar 8,192 ho gaye aur concatenation ke baad total 16,384 features fully connected layer ko milne lage. Is version mein FC1 ke 1,024 neurons the. Bernoulli rate encoding continue rahi, lekin timesteps 10 se increase karke 30 kiye gaye. Version 0.3 mein IF-like neuron behavior investigate hua, jabke Version 0.4 mein beta 0.9 ke saath LIF neurons use kiye gaye, taake membrane potential gradually decay ho aur previous information ka influence control ho sake. Training configuration mein Adam ki jagah SGD optimizer aur focal loss ki jagah standard cross-entropy loss use hua. Batch size bhi 2 rakha gaya. Lekin LIF introduce karne ke baad bhi model ki validation accuracy approximately 5.85–5.98% ke aas-paas rahi aur final output neurons meaningful spikes generate nahi kar rahe the. Further investigation mein membrane potential, gradient norms aur gradient clipping analyze ki gayi. Results se pata chala ke gradients calculate ho rahe the, lekin output neurons threshold cross nahi kar pa rahe the. Isliye ye versions mainly model ke learning behavior aur spike-generation problems ko investigate karne ke liye important the, na ke successfully improved classification accuracy demonstrate karne ke liye.
